      "Workshops - What RACI Hat Owns This Workshop?": [
        {
          "id": "spf:client-kickoff-workshop-template",
          "label": "Client Kickoff Workshop Template"
        }
      ],
      "Duty Description": "The Business Analysis duty turns fuzzy requests into a clear, shared picture of what to build. Analysts gather requirements, write user stories and acceptance criteria, and shape problem statements so everyone agrees on what needs to happen and how they will know it is done. In agile work they write just enough to get moving and keep refining as the team learns.",
      "What Does It Take for This Duty To Succeed?": "It takes a knack for asking good questions and translating between people, plus skills like requirements management, writing user stories, and defining acceptance criteria. The strongest analysts pair that with patience, active listening, and the facilitation skills to get a room to agree.",
      "Why Is This Duty Important to Project Success?": "Clear requirements are one of the biggest reasons projects succeed or quietly fail. This duty produces the acceptance criteria and user stories the whole team builds against, so designers and developers stop working from different assumptions and expensive rework never happens.",
      "You Might Enjoy This Duty If...": "You might enjoy this duty if you like untangling messy problems, enjoy detail, and are good at translating between what people say they want and what the team can actually build.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "Atlassian Agile Coach, with guides on agile, Scrum, and Kanban: https://www.atlassian.com/agile"
    },
