      ],
      "Duty Description": "The Product Management duty sets the direction for a product, the what and the why behind the work. Managers dig into users and the market, shape the vision and strategy, and rally the team around which problems are worth solving. They do not build it all themselves; they help everyone pull in the same direction.",
      "What Does It Take for This Duty To Succeed?": "It takes strategic thinking, market and customer insight, and the storytelling to get people behind a vision. Because a manager works through others, the people skills, influence, negotiation, and clear communication, matter as much as the strategy itself.",
      "Why Is This Duty Important to Project Success?": "This duty makes sure the team is building something people actually want and the business can sustain. By owning the vision, roadmap, and go-to-market plan, it connects users, business, and technology so the whole project has a clear point.",
      "You Might Enjoy This Duty If...": "You might enjoy this duty if you like strategy, enjoy connecting people, business, and technology, and are comfortable making calls with incomplete information.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "Atlassian's guide to product management: https://www.atlassian.com/agile/product-management"
    },
