        {
          "id": "spf:agile-maturity-measurements",
          "label": "Agile Maturity Measurements"
        }
      ],
      "Duty Description": "The Scrum Master duty helps a team run smoothly using agile methods like Scrum. Rather than managing people, scrum masters facilitate the rhythm of the work, sprint planning, retrospectives, and demos, and clear roadblocks so the team can focus. A lot of the job is protecting the process and helping the team keep improving.",
      "What Does It Take for This Duty To Succeed?": "It takes facilitation skills, a solid grasp of Scrum, and the patience to guide without controlling. The best scrum masters are strong listeners and conflict-resolvers who help a team surface problems and fix them together.",
      "Why Is This Duty Important to Project Success?": "This duty keeps an agile team's engine running. By facilitating sprints and retrospectives, it helps the team deliver in steady cycles and get a little better each time, which is the whole point of working in an agile way.",
      "You Might Enjoy This Duty If...": "You might enjoy this duty if you like helping a team work well together, enjoy facilitating over directing, and find satisfaction in removing the obstacles that slow people down.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "Atlassian Agile Coach, with guides on agile, Scrum, and Kanban: https://www.atlassian.com/agile"
    },
    {
