      ],
      "Duty Description": "The Project Management duty keeps the work organized and moving. Project managers track what needs to happen, watch the schedule and risks, and keep clients and teammates in the loop so nothing important slips. Much of the job is communication and clearing roadblocks before they slow the team down.",
      "What Does It Take for This Duty To Succeed?": "It takes organization, clear communication, and the ability to stay calm when a lot is in motion. Skills like project management, meeting facilitation, and stakeholder management help, along with the people sense to keep everyone aligned.",
      "Why Is This Duty Important to Project Success?": "This duty is the glue that holds a project together. By tracking milestones, managing risk, and keeping the client relationship healthy, it lets the rest of the team focus on the work instead of the logistics.",
      "You Might Enjoy This Duty If...": "You might enjoy this duty if you like structure, enjoy helping others do their best work, and stay level-headed when things get busy.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "Atlassian Agile Coach, with guides on agile, Scrum, and Kanban: https://www.atlassian.com/agile"
    },
