      ],
      "Duty Description": "The Development duty builds the product, turning designs and requirements into working software. Developers write and document code, build APIs and databases, and deploy what they make so it runs the way it should. It is problem-solving work, breaking a big challenge into small pieces and getting each one working, often in short cycles alongside the rest of the team.",
      "What Does It Take for This Duty To Succeed?": "It takes solid technical skills, programming, database work, and API design, plus the logical thinking to debug problems methodically. The strongest developers also collaborate well, since building software is a team sport that depends on shared ownership and clear communication.",
      "Why Is This Duty Important to Project Success?": "This duty is where the product actually gets made. The code, APIs, and databases it produces are the working thing users rely on, so the care put in here shows up directly in whether the product holds together.",
      "You Might Enjoy This Duty If...": "You might enjoy this duty if you like logic and building things, enjoy solving technical puzzles, and feel real satisfaction when something you made finally runs.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "MDN Web Docs, a trusted resource for building software: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn"
    },
