        },
        {
          "id": "spf:database-architecture",
          "label": "Database Architecture"
        }
      ],
      "Duty Description": "The Solutions Architecture duty designs the technical foundation a product is built on. Architects map out how the system fits together, its databases, services, network, and hosting, so developers have a solid, scalable base to build against. It is big-picture technical work that shapes how well everything else holds up.",
      "What Does It Take for This Duty To Succeed?": "It takes deep systems thinking and strong skills in database and network architecture, plus the ability to weigh trade-offs and explain them clearly. Good architects balance what is ideal with what the team can realistically build and maintain.",
      "Why Is This Duty Important to Project Success?": "This duty sets the technical direction that everything else depends on. A sound architecture lets the product scale and stay stable, while a shaky one causes problems that surface long after launch, so getting it right early matters.",
      "You Might Enjoy This Duty If...": "You might enjoy this duty if you like seeing the whole system at once, enjoy solving structural puzzles, and care about building something that will hold up as it grows.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "MDN Web Docs, a trusted resource for building software: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn"
    },
    {
      "id": "spf:information-security-analysis",
      "type": [
        "schema:DefinedTerm",
        "spf:Duty",
