          "id": "spf:network-architecture",
          "label": "Network Architecture"
        }
      ],
      "Duty Description": "The Information Security Analysis duty protects a product and its users from threats. Analysts model how something could be attacked, test for weaknesses, configure defenses, and audit the system to keep data safe. It is careful, detail-driven work that looks for problems before someone with bad intent does.",
      "What Does It Take for This Duty To Succeed?": "It takes a security mindset, network knowledge, and the patience to probe a system for weak spots. Strong analysts pair technical skill with clear communication, since much of the job is explaining risks in a way the team can act on.",
      "Why Is This Duty Important to Project Success?": "This duty keeps trust intact. A single security gap can undo a lot of good work and harm the people a product serves, so by finding and closing weaknesses early, this duty protects both users and the team's reputation.",
      "You Might Enjoy This Duty If...": "You might enjoy this duty if you like thinking like a puzzle-solver, enjoy finding weak spots others miss, and care about keeping people and their data safe.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "OWASP, the open community for software security: https://owasp.org/"
    },
