      ],
      "Duty Description": "The UX Writing duty crafts the words inside a product, the buttons, labels, messages, and instructions that guide people along. Writers shape a clear voice, build style guides, and cut anything confusing so the product feels simple to use. It sounds small, but the right words can make or break whether people understand what to do.",
      "What Does It Take for This Duty To Succeed?": "It takes a love of clear language, strong writing and editing skills, and an eye for how words fit into a design. Add empathy and collaboration, since good UX writing comes from understanding users and working closely with designers and researchers.",
      "Why Is This Duty Important to Project Success?": "This duty is what makes a product feel clear instead of confusing. Its words appear at every step users take, so strong writing quietly guides people through the experience and reduces the friction that makes them give up.",
      "You Might Enjoy This Duty If...": "You might enjoy this duty if you love words, care about making things easy to understand, and enjoy finding the simplest way to say something.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "Nielsen Norman Group, a trusted source for UX research and design: https://www.nngroup.com/"
    },
