      ],
      "Duty Description": "The Agile Coaching duty helps teams work better together, not by managing them but by guiding how they collaborate. Coaches teach agile ways of working, run workshops, and help a team build trust, ownership, and steady improvement. Much of the job is noticing how people interact and gently helping them get unstuck.",
      "What Does It Take for This Duty To Succeed?": "It takes strong coaching and facilitation skills, deep familiarity with agile methods, and the patience to guide rather than direct. The best coaches lead with empathy and read a team's dynamics well enough to know when to step in and when to hold back.",
      "Why Is This Duty Important to Project Success?": "This duty raises the whole team's ceiling. By helping people collaborate, take risks, and keep improving, it turns a group of individuals into a real agile team, which is what makes everything else on a project work better.",
      "You Might Enjoy This Duty If...": "You might enjoy this duty if you care about people's growth, like facilitating more than directing, and find satisfaction in watching a team come into its own.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "Atlassian Agile Coach, with guides on agile, Scrum, and Kanban: https://www.atlassian.com/agile"
    },
