        {
          "id": "spf:qa-analysis",
          "label": "QA Analysis"
        }
      ],
      "Duty Description": "The QA Analysis duty makes sure the product actually works before it reaches users. QA analysts write test plans and cases, put the product through its paces, and catch bugs and broken flows while they are still cheap to fix. In agile work they test continuously, checking each piece as it is built rather than waiting until the very end.",
      "What Does It Take for This Duty To Succeed?": "It takes sharp attention to detail, logical thinking, and the discipline to test methodically, plus skills like writing BDD scenarios and QA test plans. The best analysts stay curious about how something might break and communicate the issues they find clearly.",
      "Why Is This Duty Important to Project Success?": "This duty protects quality and trust. Shipping something broken costs far more than catching it early, so by finding problems before launch, QA keeps the product reliable and the team's reputation intact.",
      "You Might Enjoy This Duty If...": "You might enjoy this duty if you like finding the flaw everyone else missed, enjoy methodical work, and take pride in making sure things really work.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "MDN Web Docs, a trusted resource for building software: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn"
    },
