      "Responsible Deliverables": [
        {
          "id": "spf:logo-and-brand-assets",
          "label": "Logo and Brand Assets"
        }
      ],
      "Duty Description": "The Graphic Design duty creates the visual pieces that give a product its personality, logos, icons, illustrations, and brand assets. Designers turn ideas into clean, recognizable visuals that help a product look polished and feel like itself. It is craft-focused work where small details add up to a strong overall impression.",
      "What Does It Take for This Duty To Succeed?": "It takes visual craft, an eye for hierarchy and detail, and skills like icon design and illustration. Add collaboration and openness to feedback, since visuals usually go through several rounds before they feel right.",
      "Why Is This Duty Important to Project Success?": "This duty shapes how a product looks and feels at first glance. Strong visuals build trust and make a product memorable, tying the whole experience together so it feels professional and complete.",
      "You Might Enjoy This Duty If...": "You might enjoy this duty if you love visual craft, enjoy making things look clean and clear, and get satisfaction from polishing details until they feel right.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "Nielsen Norman Group, a trusted source for UX research and design: https://www.nngroup.com/"
    },
