          "id": "spf:customer-experience-strategy-workshop-template",
          "label": "Customer Experience Strategy Workshop Template"
        }
      ],
      "Duty Description": "The UX Strategy duty connects the day-to-day design work to the bigger picture of the user experience. Strategists map user journeys, storyboard experiences, and shape how the whole product should feel over time, so individual screens add up to a coherent journey. It is high-level thinking that keeps design pointed at real user and business goals.",
      "What Does It Take for This Duty To Succeed?": "It takes strong strategic and systems thinking, an understanding of the full customer experience, and the ability to zoom out from single screens to the whole journey. Add advocacy and business sense to connect user needs with what the organization is trying to achieve.",
      "Why Is This Duty Important to Project Success?": "This duty keeps design decisions aligned with a bigger goal instead of happening piece by piece. By mapping the journey and setting experience strategy, it makes sure the many parts of a product add up to something that genuinely works for users.",
      "You Might Enjoy This Duty If...": "You might enjoy this duty if you like seeing the big picture, enjoy connecting the dots between user needs and business goals, and prefer shaping direction over polishing details.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "Nielsen Norman Group, a trusted source for UX research and design: https://www.nngroup.com/"
    },
