        {
          "id": "spf:backlog-management-workshop-template",
          "label": "Backlog Management Workshop Template"
        }
      ],
      "Duty Description": "The Product Operations duty sets up how a team actually works together. Ops people define working agreements, map team processes, choose the right agile method, and clarify who owns what, so the team runs smoothly instead of tripping over itself. It is the behind-the-scenes work that makes good collaboration possible.",
      "What Does It Take for This Duty To Succeed?": "It takes process thinking, facilitation, and a good feel for team dynamics, plus skills like agile method selection and defining working agreements. The best ops people balance structure with flexibility, since a process should help a team, not box it in.",
      "Why Is This Duty Important to Project Success?": "This duty is what lets a team scale and stay healthy. By defining clear processes and agreements, it reduces confusion and conflict, freeing everyone else to focus on the actual work rather than on how to work together.",
      "You Might Enjoy This Duty If...": "You might enjoy this duty if you like building systems that help people work better, enjoy smoothing out friction, and get satisfaction from a team that runs well.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "Atlassian Team Playbook, practical plays for healthy teamwork: https://www.atlassian.com/team-playbook"
    },
