      "Responsible Deliverables": [
        {
          "id": "spf:statement-of-work",
          "label": "Statement of Work"
        }
      ],
      "Duty Description": "The Account Management duty owns the relationship with the client. Account managers keep communication clear, set expectations, and make sure the client feels heard while the team focuses on the work. Much of the job is trust-building, being the steady point of contact who keeps everyone aligned.",
      "What Does It Take for This Duty To Succeed?": "It takes strong relationship-building, communication, and business sense, plus the diplomacy to balance client wishes with what the team can deliver. Skills like stakeholder management and clear expectation-setting sit at the center of the role.",
      "Why Is This Duty Important to Project Success?": "This duty keeps the client relationship healthy, which protects the whole project. By managing expectations and communication, it prevents misunderstandings that could derail the work and builds the kind of trust that leads to lasting partnerships.",
      "You Might Enjoy This Duty If...": "You might enjoy this duty if you like working with people, enjoy being the trusted point of contact, and are good at balancing what a client wants with what is realistic.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "Atlassian Team Playbook, practical plays for healthy teamwork: https://www.atlassian.com/team-playbook"
    },
    {
      "id": "spf:everyone",
      "type": [
        "schema:DefinedTerm",
        "spf:Duty",
        "skos:Concept"
      ],
      "Duty Name": "Everyone",
      "Responsible Tasks": [
        {
          "id": "spf:creating-presentations",
          "label": "Creating Presentations"
        },
        {
          "id": "spf:creating-ai-prompts",
          "label": "Creating AI Prompts"
        }
      ],
      "Accountable Tasks": [
        {
          "id": "spf:creating-presentations",
          "label": "Creating Presentations"
        },
        {
          "id": "spf:creating-ai-prompts",
          "label": "Creating AI Prompts"
        }
      ],
      "Consulted Tasks": [
        {
          "id": "spf:creating-presentations",
          "label": "Creating Presentations"
        },
        {
          "id": "spf:creating-ai-prompts",
          "label": "Creating AI Prompts"
        }
      ],
      "Responsible Deliverables": [
        {
          "id": "spf:sprint-demo-presentation",
          "label": "Sprint Demo Presentation"
        },
        {
          "id": "spf:ai-prompt",
          "label": "AI Prompt"
        }
      ],
      "Duty Description": "The Everyone duty covers the work that is not owned by one role but shared by the whole team. Things like giving sprint demos and writing AI prompts are part of everyone's job, whatever their specialty. It is a reminder that on an agile team, some responsibilities belong to all of us.",
      "What Does It Take for This Duty To Succeed?": "It takes the shared basics of good teamwork: clear communication, presentation skills, and a willingness to pitch in beyond your own lane. Comfort with common tools and a habit of helping wherever needed go a long way.",
      "Why Is This Duty Important to Project Success?": "This duty reflects how real agile teams work, with people stepping up for shared tasks rather than staying strictly in their roles. That shared ownership is part of what makes a team resilient and keeps work from falling through the cracks.",
      "You Might Enjoy This Duty If...": "You might enjoy contributing here if you like pitching in wherever you are needed, enjoy presenting the team's work, and believe the best teams share the load.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "Atlassian Team Playbook, practical plays for healthy teamwork: https://www.atlassian.com/team-playbook"
    }
  ]
}